		{"id":"b000000000000001","type":"group","x":160,"y":160,"width":2540,"height":2040,"color":"5","label":"TOLL OPERATOR — consolidated, but commodity-priced output / low switching"},
		{"id":"b000000000000002","type":"group","x":2700,"y":160,"width":2540,"height":2040,"color":"4","label":"FORTRESS POSITION — monopoly + high switching = durable pricing power"},
		{"id":"b000000000000003","type":"group","x":160,"y":2200,"width":2540,"height":2040,"color":"1","label":"COMMODITY TRAP — pricing power must come from cycle/asset/balance sheet, not industry structure"},
		{"id":"b000000000000004","type":"group","x":2700,"y":2200,"width":2540,"height":2040,"color":"3","label":"STICKY SPECIALTY — fragmented, but integration-locked customers"},
		{"id":"b000000000000005","type":"group","x":3988,"y":180,"width":1252,"height":838,"color":"4","label":"★ APEX — elite Fortress (both axes ≥80)"},
		{"id":"a000000000000001","type":"text","text":"## Pricing Power Matrix\n\nEvery active thesis plotted on **(consolidation × switching cost)**. Y-axis (vertical) = market share concentration. X-axis (horizontal) = customer lock-in.\n\n**Quadrants** (split at 50/50):\n- 🟢 **FORTRESS** (top-right): monopoly + high switching → durable pricing power, premium multiples justified\n- 🔵 **TOLL OPERATOR** (top-left): consolidated industry but commodity output or weak lock-in → volume but capped pricing\n- 🟡 **STICKY SPECIALTY** (bottom-right): fragmented industry, locked-in customers → pricing power via specificity (often qualified per-customer or integration-deep)\n- 🔴 **COMMODITY TRAP** (bottom-left): fragmented + low switching → no pricing power; thesis must rest on cycle, asset value, balance sheet\n\n**Inner APEX zone** (consolidation ≥80 AND switching ≥80, marked top-right): elite Fortress positions where both axes are unambiguous monopolies. These are the multiples-don't-matter compounders — premium today, premium in 5 years.\n\n**Color = conviction**: green = HIGH · yellow = MEDIUM · red = LOW · grey/blank = exposure-only (no single-name conviction; BTC/GLD).\n\n**Use cases**: (1) Relative-value within quadrant — e.g., AMAT 31x P/E vs LRCX 48x in same Fortress slot raises an AMAT case. (2) Risk concentration — too many positions in one quadrant signals correlated cycle exposure. (3) Conviction-quadrant alignment — HIGH-conviction positions should cluster in Fortress; HIGH in Commodity Trap is a red flag worth diligence.","x":200,"y":-820,"width":5000,"height":560,"color":"5"},
		{"id":"a000000000000011","type":"text","text":"## SWITCHING COSTS / CUSTOMER LOCK-IN →\n\n**Left** = commodity, perfect substitutes · **Mid** = some integration · **Right** = qualified per customer, multi-year retraining, IP/data lock-in\n\n*How hard is it for the customer to switch supplier?*","x":1950,"y":4300,"width":1500,"height":160,"color":"5"},
